            <ArticleTitle>Chronic pain management in the cancer survivor: tips for primary care providers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>28-38; quiz 38-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000429893.95631.63</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many cancer survivors suffer from chronic pain related to treatment. Pain management in the survivor is similar to chronic noncancer pain, with the important caveat that new or worsening pain must be promptly assessed for malignancy. This article reviews cancer survivorship, identifies common pain problems, and discusses strategies for management.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
